{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.98,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["IC1", "L2", "C13", "Q2", "R2", "U5", "U4", "J2"],
      "pins": ["IC1.C1", "L2.2", "C13.1", "Q2.2", "R2.2", "U5.28", "U5.29", "U4.2", "J2.4"],
      "nets": ["BAT+"],
      "observed": "The net BAT+ contains the regulator's feedback pin (IC1.C1), the inductor output (L2.2), the output capacitor (C13.1), and all +3V3 loads (Q2 source, R2 pull-up, U5 3.3VD pins, U4 MIC_VDD, J2 VDD). There is no +3V3 net in the netlist.",
      "expected": "The +3V3 rail should be a separate regulated output from IC1/L2, with IC1.FB, C13, and the listed loads connected to +3V3, isolated from the BAT+ input rail.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "SW (pin B1) → L2 (1.0 µH, Murata LQM2MPN1R0MGHL) → +3V3 output rail."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "FB (pin C1) → +3V3 directly (fixed-output part; this is the standard connection for a fixed-voltage FAN53610 variant)."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "C13 (10 µF) on +3V3→GND is the output cap"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"BAT+\") ... (node (ref \"IC1\") (pin \"C1\") (pinfunction \"FB\") ... (node (ref \"L2\") (pin \"2\") ... (node (ref \"C13\") (pin \"1\") ..."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The buck regulator output is shorted to its input; the board has no regulated 3.3 V rail. The SKW92A, keyboard, microSD, and EPD power switch will see the raw battery/USB voltage (up to 4.2 V or 5 V), which can cause malfunction or damage.",
      "confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C1"],
      "pins": ["C1.1", "C1.2"],
      "nets": ["Display_Power_Switch", "GND"],
      "observed": "C1 has value \"0.1uF/16V\" and is connected between Display_Power_Switch and GND.",
      "expected": "The specification lists C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 as 1 µF/25 V, matching the PDI reference default.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "C2 default: 1 µF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V | Matches default"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C1\") (value \"0.1uF/16V\") ..."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The EPD power-switch rail has insufficient decoupling (0.1 µF instead of 1 µF) and a lower voltage rating than specified, which may cause unstable display power or malfunction of the EPD driver.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain a major power-rail anomaly: the +3V3 net is merged with BAT+, shorting the buck regulator output to its input and removing the regulated 3.3 V rail. Additionally, C1 is 0.1 µF/16 V instead of the specified 1 µF/25 V."
}

